AArch64 arm64-release-loadstore-main
(* Reduced from jit/reduced/arm64-main.reduced.asm -- critical section vs Release.
   The reader is already announced and inside its critical section. It performs
   its dereference and then Release() clears the slot with a PLAIN store.
   AArch64 permits Load->Store reordering, so the slot clear can become visible
   before the dereference has been satisfied. The reclaimer then scans the slot,
   sees 0, concludes nobody is protected and frees the object (modelled as
   poisoning `data`; the CBNZ is the `if it is safe to reclaim` branch).
   Bad outcome: the reader's dereference returns the poison. *)
{ 0:X0=data; 0:X1=lce; 1:X0=lce; 1:X1=data;
  lce=1; data=0; }
 P0           | P1              ;
 LDR X2,[X0]  | LDR X2,[X0]     ;
 STR XZR,[X1] | CBNZ X2,LSKIP   ;
              | MOV X3,#99      ;
              | STR X3,[X1]     ;
              | LSKIP:          ;
exists (0:X2=99)